, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 11587, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SEZBN832KfVYwhhPE8Ti1F", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 13391, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks and v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy. It was already healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the post-rollback status, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nThe incident lists follow-up work: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing, and confirm checkout traffic and downstream impact.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the release history and current status for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01P4MYsib7xZsnp4HfXEKLco", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N4pcD1VraQxdFFiVsfiJJC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 has previously been healthy in production, so the approval policy doesn't apply. Rolling back to v2.3.0 now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013HFCvbzQrX6QdU2hHEhUWG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The rollback is verified across all three regions. Next I'll confirm health and open the incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GULa7pZAhU3eG7BuM35sU4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SEZBN832KfVYwhhPE8Ti1F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate was 0.18). v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy in release history. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified. Post-rollback status is healthy with error rate 0.002 on v2.3.0 in all regions. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release, and confirm checkout traffic and downstream impact.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks and v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy. It was already healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the post-rollback status, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nThe incident lists follow-up work: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing, and confirm checkout traffic and downstream impact.", "type": "text"}]}]}